  ],
  "arms": "release is the standard CLI. candidate/default use ordinary scheduling in the diagnostic build. together releases the history worker at file-worker launch. alone releases the file workers only after history completes. one/two cap both pack-objects and index-pack; writer/index cap just the named process at one thread. All diagnostic arms run full validation before publication.",
  "model": "To model starting both jobs at commit selection, use together.outer - (files_start - selected) for each round, and compare to that round's native time. This removes intervening setup and assumes the concurrent durations are unchanged. It is not a measured delivery time.",
